WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.150
- Earlier this week, we asked Taylor Kenny

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.060
and his role on Chicago Fire

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.600
that if it helped him stay out of trouble

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.500
with law enforcement, so what about you?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.870
Have you ever had any,
any luck in that area?

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.790
- I don't get pulled over a lot.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.720
I don't get a lot of experience
with law enforcement,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.860
but the last time I was
pulled over, I was speeding,

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.700
and he said, you know,
it was that whole thing,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.960
do you know why I pulled you over?

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.140
I said, yes I do, I said, I was speeding,

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.240
I said, but here's the other thing,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.030
I left the house without
my wallet this morning,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:29.752
I don't have any government issued ID.

00:00:29.752 --> 00:00:31.330
- Oh!

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.680
- But nothing government issued

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.392
and he said, well, I, I
think I recognize you.

00:00:35.392 --> 00:00:37.030
You're an actor, right?

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.791
I said, yes sir, I'm
actually a very good actor.

00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:41.131
(laughter)

00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:43.090
He said, well, if you
give my wife an autograph,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.020
I'll let you off with a
warning, you've been very honest

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.000
and you seem, you know,
you seem to have regrets.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.500
I said, absolutely, what's her name?

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.670
He said, it's Lily.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.980
I start writing an autograph to Lily.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:53.813
He calls his wife,

00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:55.740
says, hey honey, I'm
getting you an autograph,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.090
I write, all my love,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.890
he says, it's Jason Bateman,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.517
I write Jason Bateman.

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:01.539
- What?

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:03.931
(laughter)

00:01:03.931 --> 00:01:04.952
Oh my God.

00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:07.619
You totally wrote Jason Bateman?

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.210
- I don't know.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.740
Everybody came out a win.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.666
- Oh my God, that's awesome.

00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:17.540
- [Man] The officer's
happy, everybody's happy.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.232
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's awesome.

00:01:19.232 --> 00:01:21.200
- I bet you imagine, somewhere,
Jason Bateman's happy too.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.200
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's
amazing, that's so awesome.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.300
Somewhere, Jason Bateman
gets pulled over by a cop,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.760
hey, I pulled you over,
he's like, no you didn't.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.040
(laughter)

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:29.890
I don't know you.

